{
  "title": "Namaz of Imam al-Jawad (a.s.)",
  "data": "Upon concluding the prayer, say the following supplication:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ رَبَّ الْاَرْوَاحِ الْفَانِيَةِ\nALLAAHUMMA RABBAL ARWAAHIL FAANIYAH\nO Allah, Lord of the souls passing away\nوَالْاَجْسَادِ الْبَالِيَةِ\nWAL AJSAADIL BAALIYAH\nand the rotten corpses!\nاَسْاَلُكَ بِطَاعَةِ الْاَرْوَاحِ الرَّاجِعَةِ اِلٰى اَجْسَادِهَا\nAS'ALUKA BITAA'ATIL ARWAAHIR RAAJI'ATI ILAA AJSAADIHAA\nI beseech You in the name of the obedience of the souls that are restored to their bodies\nوَبِطَاعَةِ الْاَجْسَادِ الْمُلْتَئِمَةِ بِعُرُوْقِهَا\nWA BITAA'ATIL AJSAADIL MULTA'IMATI BI-U'ROOQIHAA\nand the obedience of the corpses that join their veins\nوَبِكَلِمَتِكَ النَّافِذَةِ بَيْنَهُمْ\nWA BIKALIMATIKAN NAAFIDHATI BAYNAHUM\nand in the name of Your Word that is effective on them\nوَاَخْذِكَ الْحَقَّ مِنْهُمْ\nWA AKHDHIKAL HAQQA MINHUM\nand in the name of Your judging justly among them;\nوَالْخَلَائِقُ بَيْنَ يَدَيْكَ\nWAL KHALAA'IQU BAYNA YADAYK\nwhile the [other] creatures are standing before You\nيَنْتَظِرُوْنَ فَصْلَ قَضَائِكَ\nYANTAZIROONA FASLA QADAA'IK\nawaiting the decisions of Your judgment,\nوَيَرْجُوْنَ رَحْمَتَكَ وَيَخَافُوْنَ عِقَابَكَ\nWA YARJOONA RAHMATAKA WA YAKHAAFOONA I'QAABAK\nhoping for Your mercy, and fearing Your punishment;\nصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nSALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\n(please do) send blessings to Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَاجْعَلِ النُّوْرَ فِيْ بَصَرِيْ\nWAJ'ALIN NOORA FEE BASAREE\nplace light in my sight,\nوَالْيَقِيْنَ فِيْ قَلْبِيْ\nWAL YAQEENA FEE QALBEE\nstrong belief in my heart,\nوَذِكْرَكَ بِاللَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِ عَلٰى لِسَانِيْ\nWA DHIKRAKA BIL LAYLI WAN NAHAARI A'LAA LISAANEE\nand reference to You night and day on my tongue,\nوَعَمَلًا صَالِحاً فَارْزُقْنِيْ\nWA A'MALAN SAALIHAN FARZUQNEE\nand provide me with a righteous deed.",
  "merits": "In his book of Jamal al-Usbu', Sayyid Ibn Tawus has recorded a special prayer and supplication for each of the Holy Imams (a.s.), to be offered on Fridays.\nThis prayer consists of two units in each of which [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) is recited once and [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) is repeated seventy times."
}
